From: cizar-szymon <szymon@cs-lab.eu>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:05:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] Amiga: VQA movie sound through a stream tracker (FIFO)
 in the mixer; movies on by default; AHI ring of 4 sounds

- vqaaudio_amiga.cpp: the loader's audio data goes into a byte FIFO of a stream tracker drained by the mixer task
  (no block hand-over between the tasks; the OpenAL style ring deadlocked here). Played through Paula only: with AHI
  (warp.audio, Amiga 2) the machine froze after seconds to a minute of movie sound, cause not found, so with AHI the
  movies stay silent unless PROGDIR:vqaahi exists.
- soundio_amiga.cpp: AHI output as a ring of 4 sounds like Settlers (was 2); stream tracker API; Amiga_Sound_Backend.
- video_amiga.cpp: movies play by default, PROGDIR:nomovies or tool type MOVIES=OFF skips them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
